        "self_translation": {
          "burton_span": null,
          "status": "none"
        },
        "source": {
          "author": null,
          "basis": null,
          "locus": null,
          "status": "unidentified",
          "verified": false,
          "work": null
        },
        "text": "Whence comes this heat in the waters that burst from the moist earth? / Here Love once, at play, dipped his fiery darts; / and, delighting in the strange hissing, 'Boil on for ever,' / he said, 'and let these be the monuments of my quiver.' / Since then it boils, and rare is the guest who bathes here / whose breast gentle love does not tickle.",
